\title{A tool run that prints nothing is not a success}
\taxon{Insight}
\date{2026-11-23}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{schrodingerzy}
\tag{tooling}
\tag{process}
\import{base-macros}

\p{Source: session [ses-9U0D](ses-9U0D), on \pr{1}.}
\ul{
\li{With \code{\verb~|LD_PRELOAD~} set as in [ins-LF91](ins-LF91), \code{\verb~|lake lean File.lean~} printed nothing, and eight goals were reported as proved by Canonical. The process had died with a segmentation fault, status 139, before printing anything; the status was hidden because the output went through a pipe to \code{\verb~|grep~}.}
\li{When trying a tactic or a tool, put a command with known output in the same file, such as \code{\verb~|#eval 1 + 1~} or a goal that must fail, and read the exit status of the Lean process itself, not of the last command of a pipe.}
\li{Do not record a tool as working until a proof it found has been compiled without it or printed.}
}
